/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# The local operator file holds permissions and machine-specific paths. It is
# written by `estigia setup` and must never be committed.
estigia.local.md

# Agent skills are installed globally now, not per checkout, so neither the
# skills nor a lockfile pinning them belongs here. The paths stay listed: a run
# that installs into the checkout again should be ignored, not committed.
/.agents/skills/
/.claude/skills/
__pycache__/

# `cargo mutants` output: run logs, per-mutant diffs and a baseline, ~6 MB of it,
# regenerated by every run. It also carries absolute paths from the machine that
# produced it — `C:\Users\<name>\.cargo\registry\…` — which is a working
# directory published as though it were a fact about the crate.
/mutants.out/
/mutants.out.old/

# The working log. It is a real working document and it stays on the machine
# that keeps it: it is written in Spanish, which this repository's own rule
# forbids for anything published here, it carries absolute paths from the
# operator's own profile, and it weighs other tools by name. None of those
# belong in a repository somebody else clones.
/HANDOFF.md

# Per-session state written into the checkout by an editor plugin, one file per
# session and none of it ours. Committing it publishes the session identifiers
# of whoever happened to be running, and the directory refills on every run.
/.opencode/opencode-loop/
